" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-chevron-down" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m6 9 6 6 6-6"></path></svg></summary><div><a href="/nyc/brooklyn/">Brooklyn</a><a href="/nyc/manhattan/">Manhattan</a><a href="/nyc/brooklyn/#williamsburg">Williamsburg &amp; DUMBO</a><a href="/nyc/manhattan/#midtown">Midtown &amp; Chelsea</a></div></details><a href="/nyc/projects/">Projects</a><a href="/nyc/about/">About</a><a href="/nyc/resources/">Resources</a></nav><a class="btn primary header-quote" href="/nyc/contact/">Request a quote <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="17" height="17" viewbox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-arrow-up-right" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M7 7h10v10"></path><path d="M7 17 17 7"></path></svg></a><details class="export-mobile"><summary>Menu</summary><nav><a href="/nyc/">Home</a><a href="/nyc/products/">Products</a><a href="/nyc/interior-signs/">Interior Signs</a><a href="/nyc/exterior-signs/">Exterior Signs</a><a href="/nyc/vehicle-wraps/">Vehicle Wraps</a><a href="/nyc/custom-signs/">Custom Signs</a><a href="/nyc/trade-show-displays/">Trade Show Displays</a><a href="/nyc/retractable-banners/">Retractable Banners</a><a href="/nyc/brooklyn/">Brooklyn</a><a href="/nyc/manhattan/">Manhattan</a><a href="/nyc/projects/">Projects</a><a href="/nyc/gallery/">Gallery</a><a href="/nyc/resources/">Resources</a><a href="/nyc/contact/">Contact</a></nav></details></div></header><div class="product-ribbon"><div class="wrap"><a href="/nyc/interior-signs/">Interior signs</a><a href="/nyc/exterior-signs/">Exterior signs</a><a href="/nyc/vehicle-wraps/">Vehicle wraps</a><a href="/nyc/custom-signs/">Custom signs</a><a href="/nyc/trade-show-displays/">Trade show displays</a><a href="/nyc/retractable-banners/">Retractable banners</a></div></div><main><section class="wrap product-hero"><div><p class="breadcrumb"><a href="/nyc/">New York</a> / Storefront signs that make your entrance clear</p><p class="eyebrow">VISION GRAPHICS · NEW YORK</p><h1>Storefront signs that make your entrance clear</h1><p class="lead">Your storefront is a small but important piece of the street. The sign should tell people who you are, where to enter and why the place is relevant to them, without asking them to read an entire brochure. For New York shops, restaurants and service businesses, Vision Graphics can help coordinate the primary identity with window and door graphics. Start with the whole facade and the pedestrian approach so each element has a purpose and the entrance remains easy to recognize.</p><div class="hero-actions"><a class="btn primary" href="#request-quote">Discuss your project <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="17" height="17" viewbox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-arrow-up-right" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M7 7h10v10"></path><path d="M7 17 17 7"></path></svg></a><a class="text-link" href="#options">Explore options <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="16" height="16" viewbox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-arrow-right" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12h14"></path><path d="m12 5 7 7-7 7"></path></svg></a></div></div><figure class="project-image product-photo"><img src="/nyc/assets/mcs-new-building-signage-storefronts-960.webp" srcset="/nyc/assets/mcs-new-building-signage-storefronts-480.webp 480w, /nyc/assets/mcs-new-building-signage-storefronts-960.webp 960w" sizes="(max-width: 700px) 100vw, 50vw" alt="Signage example related to Storefront signs that make your entrance clear" loading="lazy"><figcaption>Illustrative sign example · Michigan Custom Signs source</figcaption></figure></section><section class="wrap section article-layout"><article><section><h2>Assign a role to each element</h2><p>Use the main sign for identity, the window for a focused offer and the door for practical details. Repeating the same long message on every surface can make a frontage harder to understand. Check the design at street scale and from the angle most people first see it.</p></section><section><h2>Bring the landlord into the plan</h2><p>Collect any existing sign criteria, approved sign area and restrictions on attachment or lighting. Note whether an old sign will be removed and what condition may remain behind it. Coordinate the final design with the property team before production and confirm installation responsibilities separately.</p></section><section><h2>Plan the sign and the building together</h2><p>A storefront sign needs to fit both your brand and its surroundings. Start with a straight-on building photo, a wider street view, available dimensions and your logo. Consider how the sign will read to pedestrians and people across the street. Tell us about lighting preferences, an existing sign and building management requirements. Size, construction, mounting, removal and access influence the scope. We will review the proposed approach and confirm the responsibilities for design, fabrication, approvals and installation before the project moves ahead.</p></section><section id="options"><p class="eyebrow">MATERIALS &amp; APPROACHES</p><h2>Find the right fit.</h2><div class="options-grid"><div><h3>Fascia and panel concepts</h3><p>Frame the business name within the available storefront sign area.</p></div><div><h3>Dimensional identity</h3><p>Explore raised letters or logos where the facade and approvals allow.</p></div><div><h3>Coordinated glass graphics</h3><p>Connect the main identity with hours, services and promotional messaging.</p></div></div></section><section><h2>Where it can work</h2><ul class="check-list"><li><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="18" height="18" viewbox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-check" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 6 9 17l-5-5"></path></svg>Independent retail</li><li><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="18" height="18" viewbox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-check" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 6 9 17l-5-5"></path></svg>Cafés and bodegas</li><li><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="18" height="18" viewbox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-check" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 6 9 17l-5-5"></path></svg>Salons and neighborhood services</li></ul></section><section class="faqs"><h2>A few useful answers.</h2><details><summary>Can a new storefront reuse an old sign area?<span>+</span></summary><p>Possibly, but dimensions, condition, mounting and property approvals need review. An existing sign does not establish suitability for a replacement.</p></details><details><summary>How much text should be on the main sign?<span>+</span></summary><p>Prioritize the business identity and a short descriptor when needed. Put detailed offers where pedestrians have time to read them.</p></details><details><summary>What should I send to get a storefront-sign quote?<span>+</span></summary><p>Send your logo, photos of the storefront, approximate sign dimensions, the address and your desired timing. Include any landlord criteria or existing sign drawings you have. Let us know whether an old sign needs removal and whether you want to discuss an illuminated option.</p></details><details><summary>How are building approvals and installation handled?<span>+</span></summary><p>We review the building requirements and proposed mounting approach with the project details. Access, any lighting work and the responsibilities for required approvals need to be agreed before production. Your proposal should clearly identify the included installation scope and any work assigned to other parties.</p></details></section></article><aside class="product-aside"><p class="eyebrow">LET’S START WITH THE DETAILS</p><h3>Have a space in mind?</h3><p>A photo, a few measurements and your project ZIP help us ask the right questions.</p><a href="/nyc/contact/?photo=1" class="btn dark"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="17" height="17" viewbox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-camera" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M13.997 4a2 2 0 0 1 1.76 1.05l.486.9A2 2 0 0 0 18.003 7H20a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v9a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H4a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V9a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h1.997a2 2 0 0 0 1.759-1.048l.489-.904A2 2 0 0 1 10.004 4z"></path><circle cx="12" cy="13" r="3"></circle></svg> Send a project photo</a><hr><h3>Related possibilities</h3><a href="/nyc/window-graphics/">Window graphics<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="15" height="15" viewbox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-arrow-up-right" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M7 7h10v10"></path><path d="M7 17 17 7"></path></svg></a><a href="/nyc/building-signs/">Building signs<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="15" height="15" viewbox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-arrow-up-right" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M7 7h10v10"></path><path d="M7 17 17 7"></path></svg></a><a href="/nyc/restaurants/">Restaurants<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="15" height="15" viewbox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-arrow-up-right" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M7 7h10v10"></path><path d="M7 17 17 7"></path></svg></a><a href="/nyc/r